 "answer_text": "Found 1 gene record for Huntington disease: huntingtin [1]. \n\nThe gene record for Huntington disease is NCBIGene:3064, corresponding to the gene named huntingtin [1]. Huntington disease is inherited in an autosomal-dominant pattern and is described as a monogenic neurodegenerative disorder, with principles of genetic testing discussed in the current literature [2]. \n\nClinical Features\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Chorea [3], Depression [4], Gliosis [5], Rigidity [6], Seizure [7], Hyperreflexia [8], Bradykinesia [9], Personality changes [10], Abnormality of eye movement [11] and Dementia [12]. \n\nAlthough disease-modifying therapies are not yet available, the literature notes an ongoing search for therapeutics and biomarkers to track disease progression [2]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:3064, name: huntingtin [1]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Huntington disease [13]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease [20]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease [22]. Pubmed title: Huntington disease: When does it begin [24]. Pubmed title: What Is Huntington Disease [26]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Huntington disease [14]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Huntington disease\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Chorea [3]. Medgen clinical_features: Depression [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Gliosis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Rigidity [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Seizure [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Hyperreflexia [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Bradykinesia [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Personality changes [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Abnormality of eye movement [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Dementia [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Cerebellar atrophy [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Gait ataxia [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Neuronal loss in central nervous system [17]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Huntington Disease [18]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Prospective Huntington At Risk Observational Study [19]. Clinical trial name: Family Health After Predictive Huntington Disease (HD) Testing [21]. Clinical trial name: Bioavailability of Ubiquinol in Huntington Disease [23]. Clinical trial name: Study of Huntington Patients in Connection With European Huntington's Disease Network (EHDN) [25]. Clinical trial name: Resveratrol and Huntington Disease [27]. "
